  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Jackson described agentic AI as a major opportunity for democratizing healthcare access and said the ADVOCATE program would let patients ask heart-health questions and receive reliable support and clinical interventions (s1, s4). She said harnessing AI, advanced diagnostics, and real-time immune monitoring would give ICU clinicians tools to see what is happening inside the body during critical illness (s2). She said ARPA-H is backing teams to build human-based, AI-enabled models that can forecast drug safety and efficacy before clinical trials (s5). In 2026 statements, she said ARPA-H's IGoR would modernize how evidence is generated, shared, and validated, and that AI and computational modeling can fundamentally change how medicine safety is predicted (s7, s8).",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s4",
    "s2",
    "s5",
    "s7",
    "s8"
   ],
